WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
How Canada built its retirement savings, in five dates.
1952 to 2023

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.400
OAS, 1952
Old Age Security
A basic pension for older Canadians.
Today it is the base layer many retirement incomes start from.

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.800
RRSP, 1957
Registered Retirement Savings Plan
A tax break for people with no workplace pension.
Today it is one common way to build the private layer.

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:20.200
CPP, 1966
Canada Pension Plan
A pension earned through work and contributions.
Today it adds a layer that follows a person's work history.

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.600
TFSA, 2009
Tax-Free Savings Account
Savings that grow without tax on the growth.
Today it is a flexible place to save beside the RRSP.

6
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:31.000
FHSA, 2023
First Home Savings Account
In law: after March 2023
Savings aimed at a first home.
Today it is the newest account, built for one goal.

7
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Five accounts, one system, built a layer at a time.

8
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.000
71 years from the first account to the newest.

9
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Every date, checked at its official source.
